ain diagonal.","Only entries above the main diagonal."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a6f5845341486f3374e1af56","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"How does a diagonal matrix act on coordinates?","options":["It mixes every coordinate with every other coordinate.","It always sends every vector to zero.","It swaps all coordinates.","It scales each coordinate separately."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"369db3f7528365c8682072c5","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What is the determinant of a diagonal matrix?","options":["Always $1$.","The product of its off-diagonal entries.","The product of its diagonal entries.","The sum of its diagonal entries."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"60f3175403a99103f0ce73cf","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For two $n\\times n$ diagonal matrices, which expression equals $\\operatorname{diag}(a_1,\\ldots,a_n)\\operatorname{diag}(b_1,\\ldots,b_n)$?","options":["$\\operatorname{diag}(a_1,\\dots,a_n)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(a_1b_1,\\dots,a_nb_n)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(a_1+b_1,\\dots,a_n+b_n)$","a non-diagonal matrix"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"035f71a30be04051d22edd74","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"Which matrix is diagonal?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}0&2\\\\-1&0\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}2&0\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}2&1\\\\0&-1\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}2&0\\\\3&-1\\end{pmatrix}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d534c9d2d01ad4c95d774e8a","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_007","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is $\\det\\begin{pmatrix}2&0&0\\\\0&-1&0\\\\0&0&4\\end{pmatrix}$?","options":["$5$","$8$","$0$","$-8$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"96d37e03f7fd7cf39c6661fa","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is the trace of $\\operatorname{diag}(3,0,-2)$?","options":["$-6$","$1$","$5$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d5125a36e99e8d4efbf9c128","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_009","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $D=\\operatorname{diag}(2,5)$, what is $D\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}$?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}x+2\\\\y+5\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}5x\\\\2y\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}2x+5y\\\\2x+5y\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\begin{pmatrix}2x\\\\5y\\end{pmatrix}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"353481a3cc712d2dd6d3a0fc","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $D=\\operatorname{diag}(2,3)$ and $E=\\operatorname{diag}(4,-1)$, what is $D+E$?","options":["$\\begin{pmatrix}6&1\\\\1&2\\end{pmatrix}$","$\\operatorname{diag}(8,-3)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(6,2)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(2,3,4,-1)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3068cd1fd9e2f2cb0bbe56af","time_limit":20},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_011","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which numbers are the eigenvalues of a diagonal matrix?","options":["always all equal to $1$","the sum of its entries","exactly its diagonal entries","its off-diagonal entries"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7bdb903db1878b22675cc5ae","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_012","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What stays diagonal when two diagonal matrices of the same size are added?","options":["The sum, because off-diagonal zeros remain zero.","Only the determinant, not the matrix.","The inverse of every diagonal matrix.","Nothing unless the diagonal entries are all distinct."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5856b9a858aec70468de5d7d","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What condition makes a diagonal matrix invertible?","options":["The trace is positive.","All off-diagonal entries are one.","At least one diagonal entry is zero.","Every diagonal entry is nonzero."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4567c5419d10518355a2fbca","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_014","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"If $D=\\operatorname{diag}(2,-3,4)$ and $E=\\operatorname{diag}(5,1,0)$, what is the diagonal of $DE$?","options":["$7,-2,4$","$10,-3,0$","$5,-3,0$","$10,3,4$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fafd7f790ddae98dc75d31c0","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $D=\\operatorname{diag}(2,-1,5)$, which vector is $D(1,2,3)^T$?","options":["$(2,-1,5)^T$","$(2,1,8)^T$","$(1,-2,15)^T$","$(2,-2,15)^T$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"2ecc003f7ada528dfee29ead","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Which diagonal matrix is singular?","options":["$\\operatorname{diag}(1,-1,3)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(-2,7,8)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(4,2,1)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(2,0,5)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"46c4a7d8104852d71c0d3e8f","time_limit":30},{"id":"la_batch10_diagonal_matrix_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For $D=\\operatorname{diag}(d_1,\\ldots,d_n)$ and a positive integer $k$, which expression equals $D^k$?","options":["$\\operatorname{diag}(kd_1,\\dots,kd_n)$","$kD$","$\\operatorname{diag}(d_1,\\dots,d_n)$","$\\operatorname{diag}(d_1^{k},\\dots,d_n^{k})$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback